+    - error_message: the actual exception message — rag-api's failed branch
+      persists this as the main document's `error` and into the
+      processing/summary error subdocument. Never rely on rag-api's
+      "Processing failed" fallback.
+    - stage: the pipeline stage executing at failure time (tracked by
+      process_document's current_stage local). "processing" is the safe
+      value when the stage is genuinely unknown — the same value the
+      stale-lease sweep uses for error_stage, so the field never regresses
+      to null.
+    - retryable: deliberately derived from classify_error (transient →
+      True, permanent/unknown → False), mirroring the ACK/NACK decision in
+      run_worker. Never silently defaulted by the consumer.
+    - error: legacy key retained alongside error_message for continuity
+      with any existing consumers of the status topic.
+
+    The worker→rag-api failure-path contract test pins this key set; if you
+    add or remove a key here, update that test — that is the point of it.
+    """
+    message = str(e)
+    return {
+        "error_message": message,
+        "error": message,
+        "stage": stage or "processing",
+        "retryable": classify_error(e),
+    }
